%% SensePro+ Data Flow — One Frame's Journey
%% From capture to dashboard, showing what is kept and what is discarded.

sequenceDiagram
  participant Cam as Camera/Browser
  participant WS as WebSocket/RTSP
  participant Det as SCRFD Detector
  participant Trk as ByteTrack
  participant ReID as ArcFace Re-ID
  participant FSM as Presence FSM
  participant DB as Supabase (service role)
  participant Dash as Dashboard (RLS)

  Cam->>WS: frame (JPEG/raw)
  Note over WS: Frame held in memory only
  WS->>Det: numpy array
  Det->>Det: detect faces → bounding boxes
  Det->>Trk: detections + scores
  Trk->>Trk: IoU matching → track IDs
  
  alt Re-ID interval elapsed (30s)
    Trk->>ReID: face crop + track ID
    ReID->>ReID: ArcFace embed → 512-d vector
    ReID->>ReID: cosine search vs gallery
    ReID->>FSM: matched student_id (or unknown)
  end

  FSM->>FSM: state transition (ABSENT→PRESENT / etc.)
  FSM->>DB: INSERT/UPDATE presence_intervals
  Note over DB: Only structured data persisted
  
  DB->>Dash: Realtime push (RLS-scoped)
  
  Note over Cam,WS: ⚠ Frame is discarded after processing<br/>No image ever written to disk or database
